=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | awk -F/ '{f=$NF; if (f ~ /\./) {n=split(f,a,"."); print a[n]"\t"$0} else print "(none)\t"$0}' > /tmp/files.tsv; cut -f1 /tmp/files.tsv | sort | uniq -c
 - Bash: cut -f2 /tmp/files.tsv | while read f; do ext="${f##*/}"; case "$ext" in *.*) ext="${ext##*.}";; *) ext="(none)";; esac; git blame -w -M -C --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | awk -v e="$ext" '/^author /{sub(/^author /,""); print e"\t"$0}'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines (by `git blame -w -M -C`) for each extension:

| Extension | Top owner | Lines | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 581 | Fiona Formatter is second with 291. Their lines come from the latest "reformat js" commit. Douglas Christopher Wilson has 219. |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 | Jon Church has 72 and Douglas Christopher Wilson has 67. |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 127 | Íñigo Marquínez Prado has 95. |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | Troy Goode has 12. |
| `.gitignore` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 | Troy Goode has 1. |
| no extension | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 | This is one file. Troy Goode has 5 lines in it. |

The `.js` result depends on how the reformat commit is counted. `-w` ignores whitespace changes but not the quote changes, so Fiona Formatter still gets 291 lines. Some of those lines would probably go back to the original authors if the quote-only changes were ignored too. Troy Goode leads either way.

The counts cover only the files git tracks, and only the lines that survive at HEAD.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | while IFS= read -r f; do case "$f" in *.*) e=".${f##*.}";; *) e="(none)";; esac; git blame -w --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | awk -v e="$e" '/^author /{sub(/^author /,"");print e"\t"$0}'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{c=$1;e=$2;$1="";$2="";if(!(e in s)){s[e]=1;print e"\t"c"\t"$0}}'
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines by file extension, from `git blame -w` on tracked files:

| Extension | Top owner | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 517 |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 |
| `.gitignore` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 |
| (no extension) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 |

I only kept the top author per extension, so I can't tell you how close the runner-up is. I didn't check whether Troy Goode's `.js` lines come from the latest reformat commit (`62628c0`) or from older work. If it's the reformat, the `.js` result says who ran the reformat, not who wrote the code. I can rerun with `-w -M -C` or ignore that commit via `--ignore-rev` if you want.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: run() { git ls-files | while read -r f; do [ -f "$f" ] || continue; e="${f##*/}"; case "$e" in *.*) e=".${e##*.}";; esac; git blame -w -M -C --line-porcelain $1 -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep '^author ' | sed "s/^author //;s|^|$e\t|"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{c=$1;e=$2;if(e!=p){print;p=e}}'; }; echo "== plain (-w)"; run ""; echo "== ignoring 62628c0"; run "--ignore-rev 62628c0"
 - Bash: git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -- index.js 2>&1 | head -3; git ls-files | head -20
 - Bash: git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -- lib/index.js 2>&1 | head -3
 - Bash: git ls-files | while read -r f; do e="${f##*/}"; case "$e" in *.*) e=".${e##*.}";; esac; git blame -w -M -C --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- "$f" | grep '^author ' | sed "s/^author //;s|^|$e\t|"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{e=$2;if(e!=p){print;p=e}}'
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines per extension, from `git blame` at HEAD. I ignored whitespace changes and detected moved or copied lines:

| Type | Top owner | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| `.js` | Troy Goode | 676 |
| `.md` | Troy Goode | 116 |
| `.yml` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 127 |
| `.json` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 |
| `.gitignore` | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 |
| `LICENSE` (no extension) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 |

- **Reformat commit:** The latest commit, `62628c0`, reformatted all the JS to 4-space indent and double quotes. I excluded it from blame so it doesn't take credit for lines it only restyled. Troy Goode's `.js` count is 676 with it excluded and 581 with it included. He is the top owner either way.
- **Counts:** These are line counts per author, not shares of each type, so I haven't shown how close the runner-up is.

=== ANSWER D ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | while read f; do case "$f" in *.*) e=".${f##*.}";; *) e="(none)";; esac; git blame -w --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | awk -v e="$e" '/^author /{sub(/^author /,"");print e"\t"$0}'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1nr | awk '{c=$1; $1=""; split($0,a,"\t"); e=substr(a[1],2); if(!(e in s)){s[e]=1; tot[e]=0} n[e]=n[e]+c; if(!(e in top)){top[e]=a[2]; tc[e]=c}} END{for(e in top) printf "%s\t%s\t%d\t(of %d)\n", e, top[e], tc[e], n[e]}' | sort
 - Bash: git ls-files | while read f; do case "$f" in *.*) e=".${f##*.}";; *) e="(none)";; esac; git blame -w --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep '^author ' | sed "s/^author /$e|/"; done | python3 -I -c '
import sys,collections
d=collections.defaultdict(collections.Counter)
for l in sys.stdin:
    e,a=l.rstrip("\n").split("|",1); d[e][a]+=1
for e,c in sorted(d.items()):
    t=sum(c.values()); print(e,t,[(a,n,round(100*n/t)) for a,n in c.most_common(2)])
'
FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner of surviving lines (by `git blame -w`) for each file type:

| Type | Surviving lines | Top owner | Share | Runner-up |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` | 1202 | Troy Goode | 517 (43%) | Fiona Formatter, 291 (24%) |
| `.md` | 341 | Troy Goode | 116 (34%) | Jon Church, 72 (21%) |
| `.yml` | 383 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 (31%) | Íñigo Marquínez Prado, 95 (25%) |
| `.json` | 42 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 (48%) | Troy Goode, 12 (29%) |
| `.gitignore` | 5 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 (80%) | Troy Goode, 1 |
| no extension | 22 | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 (77%) | Troy Goode, 5 |

- **Reformat commit:** the latest commit, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", is attributed to "Fiona Formatter". That puts Fiona second on `.js` with 291 lines. I used `-w`, so whitespace-only changes don't count. Quote-style changes still do, which is why Fiona keeps those lines.
- **Small samples:** `.json`, `.gitignore` and the extensionless files have very few lines, so their owners are less meaningful.

